body:
This PR proposes an expanded v0.4 of `proof-of-liveness-requirements.md`,
building on the current upstream v0.3.

It retains the core v0.3 decisions around the Sybil-resistance/unlinkability
trade-off and the distinction between cryptographic proof and underlying
biometric assurance, while developing the document into a more
implementation- and conformance-oriented requirements specification.

Major additions include:

- explicit terminology and semantic boundaries;
- formalised context and collusion assumptions;
- Minimum Liveness and Extended Personhood profiles;
- lifecycle, expiry, suspension and revocation requirements;
- holder, session and transcript binding;
- algorithm/profile agility;
- verifier-visible failure semantics;
- privacy and correlation requirements;
- assurance and evidence boundaries;
- interoperability and conformance expectations; and
- clearer treatment of delegation as separately composed evidence.

Only `proof-of-liveness-requirements.md` is changed by this PR.

